# Feature Plan Standard

Interactive plan-first work (Plan mode, "plan feature X", "bouw X" with plan before code) follows [`.cursor/skills/feature-plan-standard/SKILL.md`](../skills/feature-plan-standard/SKILL.md).

**Does not replace** [`60-feature-pipeline.mdc`](60-feature-pipeline.mdc) or [`70-agent-dispatch.mdc`](70-agent-dispatch.mdc) — complements them. `/feature` autopilot uses `artifacts/current/*`; this rule governs Cursor Plan mode and manual plan-then-build flows.

## Hard requirements

1. **No code in plan phase** — planning is read-only until user approves Build.
2. **Phase A (Explore)** — MUST dispatch explore subagents via the **Task** tool (`subagent_type: explore`), in parallel. **BLOCKED** if the agent plans from memory without explore Task output.
3. **Phase C (Council)** — MUST dispatch council via **Task** tool (`readonly: true`), in parallel. **FORBIDDEN** to role-play all council voices in the foreground without Task agents.
4. **UI-facing features** — Phase B: 2–4 ASCII wireframe options; user choice before CreatePlan finalization.

## Tier defaults

| Tier | Explore (parallel) | Council (parallel) | Default |
|------|-------------------|-------------------|---------|
| S | 1 | 3 (1× API, 1× UX, 1× QA) | trivial single-surface |
| **M** | **2** | **3** | **yes — default** |
| L | 3 | 6 (2 per role, different angles) | UI+API, migration, admin page |
| XL | 3–4 | 9 (3 per role) | auth, privacy, epic |

**Escalate** to L: new admin page, D-lane migration, substantial UI **and** API.
**Escalate** to XL: auth/permissions, privacy/PII, payments, multi-epic scope.

Record tier in plan header. User may override tier explicitly.

## Council roles (every tier)

Three roles — instances scale by tier:

- **API / architecture** — routes, resources, migrations, thin payloads ([`47-thin-api-payloads.mdc`](47-thin-api-payloads.mdc))
- **UX / consistency** — DESIGN.md, minimal subtext ([`46-minimal-subtext.mdc`](46-minimal-subtext.mdc)), mobile ~390px
- **QA / acceptance** — testable criteria, PHPUnit / Playwright (docker e2e only) / manual

Merge council output: dedupe, severity, **max 5 blockers + 5 improvements** in plan.

## CreatePlan output

- Optional mermaid architecture diagram
- **6–8 acceptance aspects**, each **3–5 scenarios** with test tool mapping
- Implementation todos with lanes (A1/A2/W1/W2/D/T)
- Cross-reference [`25-api-no-sql-leak.mdc`](25-api-no-sql-leak.mdc) for API error handling

Reference implementation: Category Health (`/admin/categories/health`) per rules 46 and 47.

## Delivery (after approval)

- Feature branch per [`05-branch-discipline.mdc`](05-branch-discipline.mdc)
- Parallel backend/frontend when contracts allow
- Tests only in containers ([`15-run-npm-in-container.mdc`](15-run-npm-in-container.mdc), [`64-container-only-playwright.mdc`](64-container-only-playwright.mdc))
- D-lane: migrate + `db-review.md` when using orchestrated delivery
